t": "Attempt ONE question from Questions 2-6", "x0": 0.5054945054945055, "y0": 0.7156177156177156, "x1": 0.8505494505494505, "y1": 0.7288267288267288}], [{"text": "Section I\u2014- Common Module: Literary Worlds", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.06371406371406371, "x1": 0.5714285714285714, "y1": 0.0777000777000777}, {"text": "25 marks", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.09712509712509712, "x1": 0.21318681318681318, "y1": 0.10644910644910645}, {"text": "Attempt Question 1", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.11344211344211344, "x1": 0.3, "y1": 0.1258741258741259}, {"text": "Allow about 1 hour for this section", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.12975912975912976, "x1": 0.42967032967032964, "y1": 0.13908313908313907}, {"text": "Answer the question in the English Extension 1 Writing Booklet. Extra booklets are available", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.14996114996114995, "x1": 0.8879120879120879, "y1": 0.16317016317016317}, {"text": "if required.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.1717171717171717, "x1": 0.22197802197802197, "y1": 0.18492618492618493}, {"text": "Your answer will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.20901320901320902, "x1": 0.5142857142857142, "y1": 0.2222222222222222}, {"text": "= demonstrate an understanding of the ideas and values of Literary Worlds and how they", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.22377622377622378, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.2501942501942502}, {"text": "are shaped and reflected in texts", "x0": 0.1813186813186813, "y0": 0.24786324786324787, "x1": 0.43956043956043955, "y1": 0.26107226107226106}, {"text": "m= craft a sustained composition appropriate to the question, demonstrating control of the", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.27117327117327117, "x1": 0.8758241758241758, "y1": 0.28438228438228436}, {"text": "use of language.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.2874902874902875, "x1": 0.310989010989011, "y1": 0.3006993006993007}, {"text": "Question 1 (25 marks)", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.3271173271173271, "x1": 0.31758241758241756, "y1": 0.3395493395493395}, {"text": "Use Text 1 to answer this question.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.3644133644133644, "x1": 0.4186813186813187, "y1": 0.3776223776223776}, {"text": "(a) The construction of literary worlds introduces time, place and character in purposeful ways.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4063714063714064, "x1": 0.9, "y1": 0.4195804195804196}, {"text": "Reflect on Text 1 and in a sustained piece of imaginative writing, construct such a literary", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4226884226884227, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.4358974358974359}, {"text": "world. (15 marks)", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.439005439005439, "x1": 0.27692307692307694, "y1": 0.4506604506604507}, {"text": "Your response should draw on your knowledge and understanding of the module Literary", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.45765345765345766, "x1": 0.8549450549450549, "y1": 0.4840714840714841}, {"text": "World", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4825174825174825, "x1": 0.1835164835164835, "y1": 0.4926184926184926}, {"text": "(b) Critically analyse the way in which your representation of time, place and character reflect", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.5019425019425019, "x1": 0.8978021978021978, "y1": 0.5283605283605284}, {"text": "your purpose and incorporate the advice in the extract. (10 marks)", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.526029526029526, "x1": 0.6648351648351648, "y1": 0.5392385392385393}, {"text": "Question 1 continues on page 3", "x0": 0.38571428571428573, "y0": 0.6083916083916084, "x1": 0.6505494505494506, "y1": 0.6208236208236209}], [{"text": "Text 1 \u2014 Extract from the Simple act of Reading ed. Debra Adelaide", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.06993006993006994, "x1": 0.7087912087912088, "y1": 0.08236208236208237}, {"text": "\u201cReading and Secrets\u201d by Giulia Giuffre in the Simple act of Reading ed. Debra Adelaide", "x0": 0.13516483516483516, "y0": 0.11421911421911422, "x1": 0.8505494505494505, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "What is it to read? Firstly, to read anything at all with any degree of receptivity is a quick and", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.1623931623931624, "x1": 0.8879120879120879, "y1": 0.17560217560217561}, {"text": "simple therapy for narcissism, Reading offers and escape to another imagination, not simply", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.17793317793317792, "x1": 0.8758241758241758, "y1": 0.20435120435120435}, {"text": "one\u2019s own. By reading, one enters into the experience and vision of other people. This is what", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.20202020202020202, "x1": 0.8901098901098901, "y1": 0.22843822843822845}, {"text": "lends books their glamour and excitement, Until you read it, you just never really know what a", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.23465423465423466, "x1": 0.8967032967032967, "y1": 0.24786324786324787}, {"text": "book might contain or where it might lead you. Proust says that reading gives us access to", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.25874125874125875, "x1": 0.8582417582417582, "y1": 0.27195027195027194}, {"text": "places and times \u2018one might not have lived through\u2019, but, more than this, reading gives us", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.2828282828282828, "x1": 0.8549450549450549, "y1": 0.29603729603729606}, {"text": "access to people who might not otherwise have been. By ushering a way into multiple ives,", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.3061383061383061, "x1": 0.8670329670329671, "y1": 0.31934731934731936}, {"text": "reading provides relief from self. To read a book is to be released into the unbounded sea of the", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.32167832167832167, "x1": 0.9021978021978022, "y1": 0.3480963480963481}, {"text": "mind, as the body to the ocean.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.3543123543123543, "x1": 0.3824175824175824, "y1": 0.36752136752136755}, {"text": "...With reading comes an independence unknown to the child listening to a story. Suddenly the", "x0": 0.13516483516483516, "y0": 0.4024864024864025, "x1": 0.9010989010989011, "y1": 0.4156954156954157}, {"text": "unimaginative portals are unlocked and can be accessed at all times of day or night. Reading is", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.42657342657342656, "x1": 0.8978021978021978, "y1": 0.4397824397824398}, {"text": "private, personal, secret, isolated, silent. No one can tell if'a page has been read or not.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4506604506604507, "x1": 0.8296703296703297, "y1": 0.46386946386946387}, {"text": "Reading is so subversive, because there is no knowing what thought or what image will be", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.47474747474747475, "x1": 0.8626373626373627, "y1": 0.48795648795648794}, {"text": "unleashed. And it will happen unseen in one\u2019s own head, blessedly unable to be supervised.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4988344988344988, "x1": 0.8714285714285714, "y1": 0.5120435120435121}], [{"text": "Section II \u2014 Electives", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.06526806526806526, "x1": 0.34175824175824177, "y1": 0.07692307692307693}, {"text": "25 marks", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.08391608391608392, "x1": 0.21318681318681318, "y1": 0.09324009324009325}, {"text": "Attempt ONE question from Questions 2-6", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.11577311577311578, "x1": 0.5010989010989011, "y1": 0.1282051282051282}, {"text": "Allow about 1 hour for this section", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.14840714840714841, "x1": 0.42967032967032964, "y1": 0.15773115773115773}, {"text": "Answer the question in the English Extension | Writing Booklet. Extra writing booklets are", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.1686091686091686, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.18181818181818182}, {"text": "available if required.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.19036519036519037, "x1": 0.3, "y1": 0.20357420357420358}, {"text": "Your answer will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.22766122766122765, "x1": 0.5142857142857142, "y1": 0.24087024087024086}, {"text": "= demonstrate understanding of the ideas and values of Literary Worlds and how they are", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.24242424242424243, "x1": 0.8857142857142857, "y1": 0.26884226884226886}, {"text": "shaped and reflected in texts", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.2665112665112665, "x1": 0.4098901098901099, "y1": 0.27972027972027974}, {"text": "= craft a sustained composition appropriate to the question, demonstrating control of the", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.2898212898212898, "x1": 0.8758241758241758, "y1": 0.30303030303030304}, {"text": "use of language.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.3061383061383061, "x1": 0.310989010989011, "y1": 0.31934731934731936}, {"text": "Question 2 \u2014 Elective 1: Literary Homelands (25 marks)", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.3644133644133644, "x1": 0.6087912087912087, "y1": 0.3776223776223776}, {"text": "Texts offer imaginative and challenging insights into society.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.3962703962703963, "x1": 0.6263736263736264, "y1": 0.4094794094794095}, {"text": "To what extent do the texts in Literary Homelands reflect this view?", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4219114219114219, "x1": 0.6824175824175824, "y1": 0.43512043512043513}, {"text": "In your response, refer to TWO of your prescribed texts and at least TWO texts of your own", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4405594405594406, "x1": 0.8758241758241758, "y1": 0.4654234654234654}, {"text": "choosing.", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.4662004662004662, "x1": 0.2098901098901099, "y1": 0.4794094794094794}, {"text": "The prescribed texts are:", "x0": 0.16373626373626374, "y0": 0.5073815073815073, "x1": 0.36043956043956044, "y1": 0.5205905205905206}, {"text": "+ Prose Fiction \u2014 Aravind Adiga, The White Tiger", "x0": 0.16373626373626374, "y0": 0.533022533022533, "x1": 0.6329670329670329, "y1": 0.54623154